00:10:48,210 --> 00:10:51,610
Let's go on a date first and we'll take it from there.

258
00:10:51,770 --> 00:10:52,130
Exactly.

259
00:10:52,370 --> 00:10:53,170
We'll see what happens.

260
00:10:53,670 --> 00:10:54,630
So let's start slowly.

261
00:10:55,190 --> 00:10:57,390
Let's take things step by step.

262
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:58,580
All right.

263
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:00,840
So that's all the phrases that we have for you today.

264
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:05,260
I think we should listen to the dialogue one last time and we'll be back to talk a little bit more.

265
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:14,200
We've been over this a hundred times.

266
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:15,490
We are not getting a pet.

267
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:16,610
Why not?

268
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,320
Come on.

269
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:19,670
Just a cute little puppy or kitty.

270
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:22,250
Who's going to look after a dog or a cat?

271
00:11:22,650 --> 00:11:23,090
I will.

272
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:26,200
I'll feed it, bathe it and walk it every day.

273
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:28,010
We can get a Labrador or a German shepherd.

274
00:11:28,630 --> 00:11:29,990
What if we want to take a vacation?

275
00:11:30,770 --> 00:11:31,550
Who will we leave it with?

276
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:35,250
Plus, our apartment is too small for that breed of dog.

277
00:11:35,750 --> 00:11:36,150
Okay.

278
00:11:36,770 --> 00:11:39,290
How about we get a cat or a ferret?

279
00:11:39,670 --> 00:11:41,430
We're planning on having children soon.

280
00:11:42,130 --> 00:11:45,090
I don't think those animals are a good idea with a baby in the house.

281
00:11:45,650 --> 00:11:46,010
Fine.

282
00:11:46,810 --> 00:11:47,850
Let's get a bird then.

283
00:11:48,170 --> 00:11:50,330
We can keep it in its cage and teach it to talk.

284
00:11:51,050 --> 00:11:52,230
A parrot would be awesome.

285
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:53,210
I'll tell you what.

286
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:56,070
I can get you some hamsters and we'll take it from there.

287
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:56,950
Yay!

288
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:09,280
Alright Catherine, so what about pets?

289
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:10,280
Are you a big pet lover?

290
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:12,070
Do you like ferrets, hamsters, all this good stuff?

291
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:14,130
I don't like small pets.

292
00:12:14,450 --> 00:12:15,250
I love big pets.

293
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:17,160
So as a kid we had both.

294
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:20,570
My brother really loved small animals like hamsters and ferrets and things like that.

295
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:22,050
I just think they're a little bit stinky.

296
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:23,400
They kind of smell funny.

297
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:27,790
So ever since, I've always really liked big animals like dogs.

298
00:12:28,190 --> 00:12:29,290
So you are a dog person.

299
00:12:29,430 --> 00:12:30,170
I am a dog person.

300
00:12:30,270 --> 00:12:32,610
This is something interesting that we describe in English.

301
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:34,920
People say I am a dog person.

302
00:12:34,950 --> 00:12:36,030
I am a cat person.

303
00:12:36,370 --> 00:12:38,810
It's almost like it says something about your personality.

304
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:40,120
Exactly.

305
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:43,290
So if you're a dog person, it means that you prefer dogs or you like dogs.

306
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,650
If you're a cat person, you prefer cats.

307
00:12:46,170 --> 00:12:52,610
And a lot of people really like dogs but don't really like cats or they love cats and they can't stand dogs.

308
00:12:53,010 --> 00:12:53,150
Right.

309
00:12:53,920 --> 00:13:00,480
And it even gets to the point where I've heard that maybe on dates people will ask, so are you a dog person or a cat person?

310
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:01,560
I know that's how I pick dates.

311
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:02,720
Really?

312
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:03,280
What about you?

313
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:04,720
Are you a dog person or a cat person?

314
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:06,240
I'm definitely a dog person.

315
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:07,380
Good answer.

316
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:07,940
Yeah.

317
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:16,680
I think cats are, I mean they're nice and they're cuddly and I think they're very good indoor pets and a little bit more fun than maybe a hamster.

318
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:21,080
But I think dogs have more life and are more energetic.

319
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:22,700
I think cats are very lazy.

320
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:24,940
And I think sometimes cats like to play mind games.

321
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:27,980
Like they're so smart that they can control you.

322
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:29,500
That makes me uncomfortable.

323
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
All right.

324
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,400
So, well, there are a lot of other pets out there.

325
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:37,880
Some people have tarantula, some people have iguanas, other people have fish.

326
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:38,160
Or horses.

327
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:39,880
Horses.

328
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:41,280
If you have enough space, right?

329
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:46,120
So we want to know what kind of pets do you have or did you have as a kid?

330
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:46,860
That's right.

331
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:47,320
Let us know.

332
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:49,800
Our website is EnglishPod.com.

333
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:50,360
We hope to see you there.

334
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:51,800
All right.

335
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:52,800
Bye.

336
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:59,706
Bye.
